ChronicleTwoMessage
Copyright 2010 The Kosugi Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/kosugi)

ChronicleTwoMessage-Regular.ttf is a modified version of Kosugi 4.002 by MOTOYA, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory).

Changes made for ChronicleTwo, by scripts/font/build_message_font.py from the parameters in
scripts/font/message_font.json:

- The glyphs are moved onto the 16x20-pixel cell grid of Dark Chronicle's message font (1280 units an
  em, 64 a pixel), and many are rescaled, moved or slanted, their stems kept at their weight.
- Accented letters, ß, ¡, ¿, ª, º, Æ, æ, Œ, œ and the half-width quotes are composed from Kosugi's own
  glyphs; the cedilla is a stroke drawn for this font.
- The font holds only the characters the game's European and English text draws.
- It is renamed ChronicleTwoMessage.

ChronicleTwoMenu
Copyright 2020 The Libre Franklin Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/Libre-Franklin)
Copyright 2020 The Jost Project Authors (https://github.com/indestructible-type)

ChronicleTwoMenu-Regular.ttf is a modified version of Libre Franklin 3.000, with its M from Jost 3.710, both licensed
under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-LibreFranklin.txt and OFL-Jost.txt in this directory).

Changes made for ChronicleTwo, by scripts/font/build_menu_font.py from the parameters in
scripts/font/menu_font.json:

- The weight 500 instances of both variable fonts, scaled onto the texel grid of Dark Chronicle's pause menu
  (64 units a texel) and stretched 1.265 times wide.
- Every letter's outer corners are rounded, and many letters are rescaled, slanted, moved or reweighted, their
  stems kept at their weight, and their advances changed.
- The question mark is drawn for this font: a hood ending in a drop, a stem and a round dot.
- The font holds only ASCII.
- It is renamed ChronicleTwoMenu.

