Antonio 1.002 and its 6 from M+ 1p 1.062, all licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
(OFL-YanoneKaffeesatz.txt, OFL-RobotoCondensed.txt, OFL-SawarabiGothic.txt, OFL-FjallaOne.txt, OFL-Antonio.txt and
OFL-MPLUS1p.txt in this directory).

Changes made for ChronicleTwo, by scripts/font/build_menu_font.py from the parameters in
scripts/font/board_font.json:

- Weight 400 instances of the variable fonts, scaled onto the texel grid of Dark Chronicle's pause menu
  (64 units a texel), each source at its own size and width.
- Many letters and figures are rescaled, slanted, moved or reweighted, their stems kept at their weight, and
  their advances changed; the a's bowl is taller and its top shorter, the P's bowl reaches lower down its
  stem, the y's tail is cut short, the 1's flag is shorter, the 5's top bar and the top of its bowl thicker, and
  the 6's stroke leans straight into its bowl.
- The font holds only ASCII.
- It is renamed ChronicleTwoBoard.

ChronicleTwoTitle
Copyright 2010 The Kosugi Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/kosugi)

ChronicleTwoTitle-Regular.ttf is a modified version of ChronicleTwoMessage-Regular.ttf, itself a modified
version of Kosugi 4.002 by MOTOYA, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory).

Changes made for ChronicleTwo, by scripts/font/build_menu_font.py from the parameters in
scripts/font/title_font.json:

- The glyphs are scaled onto the texel grid of Dark Chronicle's title menu buttons (64 units a texel, an em of
  30.8 texels) and narrowed to 0.716 of their width.
- Many letters are rescaled, moved or reweighted, their stems kept at their weight, and their advances changed;
  the round capitals and the N, m and w are wider, the w's legs splay, the descenders are longer and the space
  narrower; accented letters follow their base letters.
- The font holds ASCII and the accented letters and marks of ChronicleTwoMessage.
- It is renamed ChronicleTwoTitle.
